# Project Rules — Archerfish Game (射水鱼游戏)

## Project
- Unity 2D game, C#, Rigidbody2D physics.
- BASE CODE SOURCE: `C:\GDIM\GDIM 33\VerticalSlice` (the original course project).
  All code in this project is refactored/rewritten from the files in that folder.
  If a reference is unclear, the original implementation can be found there.

## Coding Conventions (MANDATORY)
- Method names: PascalCase (e.g. Shoot, Move, HandleMouse).
- Private fields: _camelCase (e.g. _moveSpeed, _health).
- Use [SerializeField] for private fields that should show in the Inspector.
- No public fields for Inspector use — prefer [SerializeField] private.

## Comments (MANDATORY — the user reads Chinese)
- Add Chinese comments (// 中文注释) to EVERY method and key logic block.
- Comments must explain WHAT the code does and WHY, not just restate the code.
- Keep comments concise and clear.

## Singleton Rules
- Fix GameController's Awake: check `if (instance != null && instance != this)`
  and Destroy + return BEFORE assigning `instance = this`.
- Do NOT turn GameController into a god object: do not stuff player/enemy/
  bullet/NPC references into it.
- Prefer events (C# events / static Action) or [SerializeField] dependency
  injection over `GameController.instance.xxx` chains and FindObjectWithTag.

## Constraints
- NEVER use UnityEditor namespace in runtime scripts (breaks the build).
- Keep changes localized — do not break existing gameplay outside the task.
- Compile must succeed after each change.

## Language
- Write code and prompts in English where precise, but ALL code comments
  must be in Chinese.